# Portfolio Design System Rule

Use a calm, minimal layout language with geometric accents.

## Visual Direction
- Keep composition simple and grid-driven.
- Use one dominant primary color and one supporting secondary color.
- Use accent colors sparingly for calls to action and micro-details.
- Prefer whitespace over visual noise.

## Geometry Usage
- Geometric shapes are decorative, not content containers by default.
- Keep shape opacity and contrast low enough to protect readability.
- Reuse a small set of motifs: circle, quarter-arc, square block, dot clusters.
- Avoid adding new shape types unless they solve a clear layout purpose.

## Typography and Hierarchy
- Keep text hierarchy clear: strong heading contrast, readable body size.
- Limit line length for long text sections to improve scanning.
- Keep section titles concise and action-oriented.

## Motion Principles
- Use subtle, short-duration motion for entrance and interaction feedback.
- Avoid large movement or continuous animation loops.
- Always provide reduced-motion fallbacks.

## UX Tone
- Prioritize clarity, confidence, and professional warmth.
- Keep copy direct, concise, and in plain English.
